ay Morning @ CA Badminton ","url":"https://www.meetup.com/ca-badminton-meetup-toronto-group-gta/events/316332973/","description":":Saturday Morning Drop In\nCost $ 10 \\*\\*\\*\n\\* Included Plastic birdies, please try to have cash and pay before playing.\n\\*\\*\\*(Cash Only) (Cash Only) (Cash Only)\n\nLocation: 1370 Birchmount Rd, Unit 6\n\\*The close intersection in Birchmount Rd & Lawrence Ave.\nTime: Saturday 9:30 AM - 12 PM\n\\*\\*\\*9:30 AM- 12 PM 3 courts available\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\\*Please bring your own racquet,\n\\*Please bring indoor gym sport shoes. (Change shoes in the club)\n\\*\\*\\*\n\\*This weekly gathering is for all levels (beginner to advance) badminton players.\n\\*No outside food allowed.\n\\* This event is for the purpose of playing friendly double games and for all levels of players from beginner to advance. Please do not use this as an opportunity to do training and singles games.\nAttendance in effect -please give at least 24hr notice in advance for cancelation so others may have time to react. Late show and no-shows maybe permanently removed from group and unable to rejoin.\n\\*Only registered members can participate; visitors are not permitted. If you wish to participate, please register as a member first, and then view the event details and participation instructions.\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* ⚠️⚠️⚠️\nTo ensure efficient use of event slots and fairness, all registered participants must confirm their attendance with the group administrator before the specified deadline (if a waitlist exists). \\* Before the deadline, registered members have the right to cancel and priority. To ensure fairness, if no response is received after the deadline, the waiting list member has priority.\n\nIf you do not confirm your attendance within 72 hours before the event, or are absent, your slot may be reassigned to a waiting list candidate or a new member. This rule aims to ensure fairness and maximize the participation opportunities for all members. Since the venue cost is shared by all confirmed participants, 🛎️ those who do not attend must notify the administrator before the deadline. Failure to notify the administrator before the deadline will result in payment of the venue cost. Thank you for your understanding. \\*Please note: Failure to pay the venue cost will result in your cancellation of membership.\n\nSlot allocation is based on the order of candidate responses. To ensure fairness and better coordination, when a registered candidate cancels their slot, the administrator will send a separate notification to all candidates each time slots open. Due to limited availability, places will be allocated on a first-come, first-served basis based on response time.\n\n\\*If you need to cancel your participation, please notify the administrator at least 24 hours before the event. Late cancellations will incur venue fees. Thank you for your understanding and cooperation.\n\n\\*To ensure fairness and transparency, each participant needs to confirm individually. Members who fail to cancel their registration and complete payment within the specified time will be permanently disqualified.\n\nPlease note that if you confirm participation on behalf of another member, you will be responsible for that member's event costs.\n\nTo maintain fairness for all participants, please inform your friends that they must also confirm.\n\n\\*In the event of repeated violations, the administrator reserves the right to make the final decision.\n\nThank you for your understanding and cooperation.\n\n* After reading the event details, members can contact the administrator via message.","startDate":"2026-11-28T14:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"CA Badminton Academy","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Scarborough","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1370 Birchmount rd, unit 6, Scarborough, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"CA Badminton Meetup Toronto Group GTA","url":"https://www.meetup.com/ca-badminton-meetup-toronto-group-gta/"},"performer":"CA Badminton Meetup Toronto Group GTA"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Free event. Bello's Birthday Bash w/karaoke @ Owl's Club","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/events/316612350/","description":"# 🎂🎤 Nick's Birthday Karaoke Bash! 🎤🎂\n\n### Saturday, November 28\n\nIt is my birthday week, so of course I'm looking to celebrate the best way I know how — **with good friends, great music, and karaoke!** 🥳🎶\n\nCome out and help me celebrate at one of Toronto's most unique karaoke spots — the **legendary Owl's Club!**\n\n**IMPORTANT - cash only at this venue.**\n\n📍 **Owl's Club**\n**847 Dovercourt Road, Toronto**\n\nLocated just a short walk from **Ossington Subway Station**, the Owl's Club is a unique venue with a rich and colourful history. It's also become legendary for its **Saturday karaoke nights**, making it the perfect place for a birthday celebration.\n\n### 🎤 KARAOKE!\n\nAs always, **you can sing or just sit back, relax and enjoy the performances.** Whether you're a seasoned karaoke superstar or someone who prefers being part of the audience, everyone is welcome!\nKaraoke usually gets underway around **9:15–9:30 PM** and it can get VERY busy, so if you want to sing, **put your songs in early!** 🎶\n\n### 🎱 More than karaoke!\n\nThere are plenty of other things to do while you're waiting for your turn at the microphone:\n🎯 **Free darts**\n🎱 **Pool table**\n🏒 **Shuffleboard**\n🍻 Drinks & socializing\n🎤 And, of course, lots of karaoke!\n\n### ⏰ When to arrive\n\n**8:30 PM onward**\nNick will be there from around 8:30 PM. Come early, grab a drink, get comfortable and socialize before the karaoke gets rolling.\n**Leaving time:** Whenever you like! Stay for one song or stay until the last singer — totally up to you.\n\n### 🥳 COME HELP ME CELEBRATE!\n\nBirthdays are better with friends, so I'd love to see some familiar faces and meet some new ones too!\nThis isn't just about karaoke — it's about **getting together, meeting people, having some laughs and enjoying a fun Saturday night in Toronto.**\nSingle, partnered, married, new to the group or a longtime member — **everyone is welcome!**\n\n### 📱 Want to hear about more events?\n\nJoin our **WhatsApp group** to stay connected and learn about upcoming events.\n\n**THIS GROUP IS FOR PEOPLE WHO WANT TO BE SOCIAL AND MAKE FRIENDS — WHETHER YOU'RE SINGLE OR NOT SINGLE.**\n\nWe also organize lots of other events, including:\n🎬 Movies\n🚶 Walks\n🥾 Hikes\n🎨 Arts & Culture\n🍽️ Restaurants\n🎤 Trivia\n🎉 And plenty more!\n\n### 👍 Not sure if you can make it?\n\n**You can just show up!**\nIf you're not 100% sure about your schedule, don't feel like you have to RSVP and then cancel later. You can simply **show up on the day if you end up being free.**\n\n### 📧 Stay in the loop\n\nDon't forget to join our email list! Meetup does not send emails to everyone in the group, so this is the best way to get our weekly news and hear about upcoming events:\n[http://eepurl.com/hKt76f](http://eepurl.com/hKt76f)\n\n### 👋 Your Organizer\n\n**Nick** is the organizer for this Meetup.\nIf you need to contact him, please post a message on the Meetup wall\n\n🎂 **Come celebrate my birthday, grab the mic (or don't!), and let's make it a great night!** 🎤🥳","startDate":"2026-11-29T01:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Owls Club","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"on","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"847 Dovercourt Road, Toronto, on"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/"},"performer":"Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Citadel Contemporary Dance:  Winterreise","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-arts-and-culture/events/316310556/","description":"### Winterreise\n\n##### Laurence Lemieux & Citadel \\+ Compagnie \\| Echo Chamber\n\nA solitary traveller wanders through a frozen world of memory and longing in this **moving adaptation of Franz Schubert’s *Winterreise*.** Reimagined for violin, piano, and two voices, the production intertwines live music and dance to explore love, loss, and the search for belonging in Schubert’s timeless song cycle.\n\n***Ticket link here: ($35-$45)***\n\n(you're purchasing for the Saturday November 28th--8pm\n\nhttps://www.citadelcie.com/event/winterreise/\n\nMore info on Echo Chamber:\n\nhttps://www.echochambertoronto.com/\n\nJoin us for this 'winter journey'!!","startDate":"2026-11-29T00:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"The Citadel (The Ross Centre for Dance / Citadel + Compagnie)","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"304 Parliament St., Lower Studio, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-arts-and-culture/"},"performer":"TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Christmas in Old York! 1833 (RETURN FOR 2026)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/events/316692905/","description":"\\*\\***The Toronto History Walks Yearly Pass is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours, email**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or for signing up!\\*\\***\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticket amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n\n**If you plan on attending, please get your tickets for this event early as this tour has run for the last 3 years, and does sell out rather quickly.**\n\nSo what was it like in York in 1833 at Christmas time?\n\nThe prices of various food items and gifts on display, the gas lights creating a glow as the snow begins, places to gather, places to get a drink, like the Steamboat Hotel on Front Street, or maybe one might decide to take their best girl or guy on a stagecoach trip to High Park to watch kids speed down the hills on their skids.\n\nWhat were the traditions in old York? Maybe the residents went down to the lake and watched the nighttime fishermen spear fish for Christmas dinner. Let's take a trip around old York and see what it was like back in 1833, three months before we changed our name to Toronto in 1834.\n\nOr take a holiday trip to Kingston or Montreal to buy gifts directly from New York or London stores, fancy hats for the ladies and cigars for the men. Books and wooden toys for the kids. What about that goose in the little grocery store on King Street West of Jarvis? Candies from Britain, real home made gingerbread in the store windows.\n\nOn Christmas Eve everyone walked to St. James Cathedral for the ringing of the bells, singing, and skating over the frozen Toronto Bay to the Peninsula.\n\nThis tour explores old York. This walking tour is for all walking levels. The tour begins and ends at St. James Cathedral on King Street East at Church Street. A great way to kick off the season.\n\nThis tour has a ticketed price of $15.00.\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticket amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**","startDate":"2026-11-28T17:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"The Cathedral Church of St. James","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"106 King St E, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto History Walks","url":"https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/"},"performer":"Toronto History Walks"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"30% off The Parfumerie + Pre-Dinner + Post Dessert at The Distillery District","url":"https://www.meetup.com/experiencetoronto/events/316457083/","description":"**Note: The sale ends on September 7th at 11;59pm. Theatre tickets allow free and skip-the-line entry into The Distillery District for this show.**\n\n**On Saturday, November 28th, see** **The Parfumerie at The Distillery District**. On a snowy night in downtown Budapest, a perfumery hums with chatter, gossip, and the spark of romance. Behind elegant counters, clerks scramble through the holiday rush as a secret love ignites.Tender, sharp, and riotously funny: *Parfumerie* is a romantic comedy about yearning, connection, and the leap of faith love demands. My seat is Balcony AA9. **Purchase The Parfumerie on Saturday, November 28th at 7pm.**\n\n**COST**\nRegular: $115/$135\n\nSale: $73.50/$93.50 with code WEEKENDBOGO\n\nRush: It there are any, they will be available online at 8:00 AM that morning from $32 -$40 with [code](26RUSH26)\n\nMeetup Organizer Fee: $5\n\nTicket Policy: All sales are final.\n\n**SIGNING-UP**\n\n* **RSVP, confirming if you will join for dinner before, as reservations are required**\n* **[Purchase](https://my.soulpepper.ca/16064/16172) your own ticket for Saturday November 28th at 7pm, and post your seat number in the Comment section. I will then move you to attending.**\n* Members can also show up at the Theatre with their ticket in hand.\n\nRSVPs close 2 days prior and cancellations may result in a No Show and impact future attendance.\n\nA reminder will be sent the day before with my cell and reminder details where to meet and when.\n\n**MEETUP TIME**\n**Meet me for Dinner at: 5:15pm in front of Restaurant** **TBC** (I can only make the reservation 2 weeks prior)\n\n**Meet me for the show at: 6:45pm in the line for the Baillie Theatre inside the Young Centre for the Performing Arts in the Distillery District at 50 Tankhouse Lane**\n\n**Show Starts**: **7pm**\n\nLength: estimate 2 hours\n\n**After: meet at the same spot to chat about the show/ head out for a beverage/dessert across the street**\n\nEnjoy and please post your comments in the Event after.","startDate":"2026-11-28T22:15:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-3-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Young Centre for the Performing Arts","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"Distillery District, 50 Tank House Lane, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Experience Toronto","url":"https://www.meetup.com/experiencetoronto/"},"performer":"Experience Toronto"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"On bavarde","url":"https://www.meetup.com/north-york-french-language-meetup/events/316616451/","description":"RENCONTRE EN PRÉSENTIEL AU NORTH YORK CENTRE\n\nRejoignez-nous pour deux heures de conversation en français en personne.\n\nOÙ : North York Centre, Food Court\n(5150 rue Yonge, le batiment immediatement au nord du square Mel Lastman, métro North York)\n\nQUAND : samedi de 16h00 (4 pm) à 18h00\n\nA bientôt!","startDate":"2026-11-28T21:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"North York City Centre (same bldg as the NY Library), Food court","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"North York","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"5150 Yonge Street (WEST side!!!), next to Mel Lastman Sq., North York, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"North York French Language Meetup","url":"https://www.meetup.com/north-york-french-language-meetup/"},"performer":"North York French Language Meetup"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Bhuta Shuddhi - Purification of the Five Elements","url":"https://www.meetup.com/isha-yoga-toronto-free-meditation-classes/events/316693752/","description":"Click [here](https://innerengineering.sadhguru.org/toronto) to register\n\nBhuta Shuddhi means “purification of the five elements” (i.e. earth, water, fire, air and space) which gets to root of imbalances in the body that lead to disease. This simple practice which you can do daily reorganizes your system on the elemental level.\n\nBenefits:\nKeeps the system in harmony and balance\nPrepares the system to handle powerful states of energy\nCreates the basis to gain complete mastery over the human system\n\nAge Limit: For ages 14 and above, no prior knowledge of yoga is required.\n\nThis program is conducted by a Hata Yoga teacher trained by Sadhguru.\n\nThis is a paid program.\n\nFor ages 14 and above, no prior knowledge of yoga is required.\n\nTo Learn more: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jzSX_uBstSA","startDate":"2026-11-28T19:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Arya Samaj Mississauga","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Mississauga","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"405 Watline Ave, Mississauga, ON L4Z 1P3, Canada, Mississauga, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Inner Engineering Toronto (Isha Yoga & Meditation Classes)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/isha-yoga-toronto-free-meditation-classes/"},"performer":"Inner Engineering Toronto (Isha Yoga & Meditation Classes)"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Surya Kriya: Fire Up the Sun Within (Isha Hatha Yoga)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/isha-yoga-toronto-free-meditation-classes/events/316693741/","description":"For registration and more information, click **[here](https://innerengineering.sadhguru.org/toronto)**\n\nSurya Kriya is a potent yoga of tremendous antiquity, designed as a holistic process for health, wellness, and complete inner well-being. “Surya” means “sun,” and “kriya” means “inner energy process.” Surya Kriya activates the solar plexus to raise the samat prana, or solar heat, in the system. It also balances a person’s left and right energy channels, leading to stability of the body and stillness of the mind. This strong foundation becomes the basis to explore higher dimensions of life.\n\nTraditionally available only to select groups of yogis, Surya Kriya is offered by Sadhguru as a comprehensive spiritual practice that is ideal for the hectic pace of today’s world.\n\nThis is a hatha yoga program (physical postures) which will be taught step-by-step and guided by a teacher trained in India by Sadhguru. Once you have completed the program, you can practice on your own at home. Surya Kriya does not require previous experience with yoga.\n\nBenefits:\n\n* Develops mental clarity and focus\n* Remedies weak constitutions\n* Boosts vigor and vitality\n* Balances hormonal levels in the body\n* Prepares one for deeper states of meditation\n\nAnyone above 14 years of age can attend. No previous experience of yoga required.\n\nCost\nCAD 225\nEarly Bird CAD 200 (Expires on October 29th 2026)\n\nTiming\nSaturday, November 28th, 8:30 AM - 12:00 PM\nSunday, November 29th, 8:00 AM - 12:00 PM","startDate":"2026-11-28T13:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Best Western Plus Toronto Airport Hotel","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Mississauga","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"5825 Dixie Rd, Mississauga, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Inner Engineering Toronto (Isha Yoga & Meditation Classes)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/isha-yoga-toronto-free-meditation-classes/"},"performer":"Inner Engineering Toronto (Isha Yoga & Meditation Classes)"}]</script><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/3/9/9/7/highres_507254743.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/4/7/6/2/highres_523578274.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/2/6/a/3/highres_451449891.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/3/7/e/3/highres_499514307.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/d/7/d/6/highres_536035254.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/8/8/8/9/highres_445414953.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/c/8/f/1/highres_519291441.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic